{"type":"standard","title":"Nancy Lacore","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Nancy Lacore</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q61953884","titles":{"canonical":"Nancy_Lacore","normalized":"Nancy Lacore","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Nancy Lacore</span></span>"},"pageid":60123984,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/VADM_Nancy_S._Lacore_%282%29.jpg/330px-VADM_Nancy_S._Lacore_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/VADM_Nancy_S._Lacore_%282%29.jpg/1920px-VADM_Nancy_S._Lacore_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":3561,"height":4451},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375285822","tid":"92196cbd-b221-11f1-9ffb-8ec85981fde2","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:54:28Z","description":"U.S. Navy vice admiral and political candidate","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Lacore","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Lacore?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Lacore?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Nancy_Lacore"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Lacore","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Nancy_Lacore","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Lacore?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Nancy_Lacore"}},"extract":"Nancy S. Lacore is a retired United States Navy officer and political candidate who served as the 16th Chief of Navy Reserve from 2024 to 2025. A vice admiral, she previously served as the 93rd commandant of Naval District Washington from 2022 to 2024. She also served as the director of the Maritime Partnership Program, U.S. Naval Forces Europe/Africa/U.S. 6th Fleet, with additional duties as vice commander of U.S. 6th Fleet in Naples, Italy.","extract_html":"<p><b>Nancy S. Lacore</b> is a retired United States Navy officer and political candidate who served as the 16th Chief of Navy Reserve from 2024 to 2025. A vice admiral, she previously served as the 93rd commandant of Naval District Washington from 2022 to 2024. She also served as the director of the Maritime Partnership Program, U.S. Naval Forces Europe/Africa/U.S. 6th Fleet, with additional duties as vice commander of U.S. 6th Fleet in Naples, Italy.</p>"}